      "id": 1,
      "text": "On September 17, 1862, Antietam became the bloodiest day in American history when about 23,000 soldiers were killed, wounded, or missing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/anti/index.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Battle of Antietam ended the Confederate Army of Northern Virginia's first invasion into the North and prompted Lincoln to issue the preliminary Emancipation Proclamation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/anti/index.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 8.5‑mile driving tour and numerous hiking trails let visitors explore the Antietam battlefield at their own pace.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.battlefields.org/visit/battlefields/antietam-battlefield",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Dunker Church was rebuilt on its original site, and several family farms used during the battle remain preserved.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.battlefields.org/visit/battlefields/antietam-battlefield",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Antietam Iron Furnace Site and Antietam Village were listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1975.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antietam%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Antietam National Battlefield’s Visitor Center is a great starting point, and recent preservation work has opened up views across the center of the battlefield.",
